#
# Fairground, the cooperative market: layer 79 of the matrix. What the
# owner shares, wants and still waits on (net.offers), sharing, wanting
# and selling on the peer network (net.command share, want, sell), the
# settled sales and purchases and the fees the node paid (mesh.books, the
# peer book's settlements in peer.status), and the swarm's market (the
# money supply, pot, levy and fees of swarm.state). Every method is
# zxvd's; none is invented.
#
# Advisory and owner-confirmed (fairground_model.h FM3): a share, a want
# or a sell is only checked and held, with a notice, until the owner
# approves it; only then is net.command sent, and a cancelled one sends
# nothing. Networking is off by default and Fairground never turns it on
# or off (no "off", "lan", "online" or "peer" command): the network's
# mode is Trellis's (layer 29). Money is integer minor units of VFV, the
# peer book's unit, never a float.
#
# 6 later layers lean on this one, so its rules are general and owned
# here (CONCEPTS.tsv): the assurance fee on a sale, an offer inside the
# owner's limits, the price per unit across offers and an offer's record.
# Of the layers the task names, Coffer (73) is built before this one and
# owns the money: the wallet after a settlement is coffer.balance, used as
# it is. Vintner (91) is built before it, but its quantity_at_price is one
# price per unit, where a receipt here carries one price for all its
# units, so it does not fit. Toolchest (126) judges kits and Trellis (29)
# the mesh's devices and the network's mode, neither of which Fairground
# decides, so neither is used. Commons (27) comes after this layer in the
# build order (MATRIX_ORDER.tsv), so nothing of it is used.
#
# Witness pairs are of one kind (zxapp.c run_one B3). Sutra and Trebago
# witness the assurance fee, a number (copied from blocks/fee_check's
# shape). Eve and Sutra witness offer_allowed, a truth: Eve checks each
# field against its own range alone, so the owner's limits come as
# margins (priceroom, unitsroom) the model works out. Trebago alone gives
# the price per unit across offers, an exact rational, and Sutra the
# offer's fixed record. The model's C (fairground_rules.h) is the third
# witness of each.
#
# Planned (no runtime yet): Eiffel (design by contract) and Solidity
# (contract rules) own whether an offer may stand, the contract an offer
# makes: pending on offer_allowed. SAS (statistical reports) owns the
# price per unit across offers, a statistic over the owner's records:
# pending on offer_unit_price.
#
# Defaults taken: the owner's limits start at 0, so nothing is allowed
# until the owner sets them (fairground_set_limits); a share is checked
# only against its digits (it has no price) and still waits for the
# owner. swarm.state is the swarm's, so `swarm` is declared beside the
# task's peers, net, ledger.read and notify. zxvd has no notification
# method, so the notice is only composed for the view (fairground_t
# notice).
zxapp 1
id     fairground
name   Fairground
version 1.0.0
slot   79
layer  L1
matrix 79
icon   icons/l1/079-fairground.svg
budget 233
needs  peers
needs  net
needs  ledger.read
needs  notify
needs  swarm
model  apps/fairground_model.c
use    coffer 1   # @num.coffer_balance

# The 0.08889% assurance fee on a sale (FR1): floor(amount * 8889 / 10^7).
# Sutra holds 15 digits and refuses past them; Trebago answers to 2^53 - 1.
provides assurance_fee num amount
logic    sutra   assurance_fee apps/blocks/fairground/fee.sutra
logic    trebago assurance_fee apps/blocks/fairground/fee.tb

# An offer inside the owner's limits (FR2): price and units at least 1,
# both margins not below 0. Eve holds 9 digits as no; Sutra refuses them.
provides offer_allowed truth price units priceroom unitsroom
logic    eve   offer_allowed apps/blocks/fairground/offer.eve
logic    sutra offer_allowed apps/blocks/fairground/offer.sutra
pending  Eiffel offer_allowed
pending  Solidity offer_allowed

# The price per unit across offers (FR3), exact, in Trebago.
provides offer_unit_price num price units
logic    trebago offer_unit_price apps/blocks/fairground/unit.tb
pending  SAS offer_unit_price

# An offer's fixed business record (FR4), in Sutra.
provides offer_rec_ok truth offer kind resource units price status
logic    sutra offer_rec_ok apps/blocks/fairground/record.sutra

# Its own proof (zxapp.h K1): each entry at its edges, and where its languages disagree
check assurance_fee amount=0,1124,1125,180000,10000000,999999999999999 = 0,0,1,160,8889,888899999999
check assurance_fee amount=1,1000000000000000 = both
check assurance_fee amount=1,9007199254740991 = both
check offer_allowed price=1,999999999,0,5,5,5 units=1,999999999,1,0,1,1 priceroom=0,999999999,0,0,-1,0 unitsroom=0,0,0,0,0,-1 = true,true,false,false,false,false
check offer_allowed price=1,1000000000 units=1,1 priceroom=0,0 unitsroom=0,0 = both
check offer_allowed price=1,1 units=1,1 priceroom=0,1000000000 unitsroom=0,0 = both
check offer_unit_price price=300,400 units=2,4 = 350/3
check offer_unit_price price=0,0 units=1,1 = 0
check offer_unit_price price=7,0 units=1,1 = 7/2
check offer_rec_ok offer=0,9999,10000,1,1,1,1 kind=1,3,1,0,2,2,2 resource=1,2,1,1,3,1,1 units=0,999999999999999999,0,0,0,-1,0 price=0,999999999999999999,0,0,0,0,0 status=0,3,0,0,0,0,4 = true,true,false,false,false,false,false
# The wallet after a settlement (FM4): a want of 300 and its fee 0 paid, a sale of 500
check coffer.balance before=1000,0 moved=-300,500 = 700,500
